## Most consequential novelty decisions
The chain-ring trichotomy and exact d*h synthesis remain candidates, not a confirmed first result. The characteristic-two exact oracle bounds require comparison to de Beaudrap and modal-query literature at the same access model. Generic MQT phenomena, the single-state independence criterion, faithful-probability obstructions, polynomial-method architecture, circulant algebra, Reed-Muller radical characterization, base-change naturality and permutation-span ingredients are downgraded to background or routine application.

Two working metadata problems were resolved before delivery: the full Chimal-Dzul/Gassner/Rosenthal/Schnyder author list was verified, and the incorrect TAC locator for Cockett-Lack was replaced with the correct author-hosted Restriction categories I paper and its journal/DOI record. These are bibliographic corrections, not new mathematical evidence.
